{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":280848,"duration_api_ms":280785,"num_turns":1,"result":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: go-unix-utils is an experiment in specification-driven development. It derives formal specifications from C source code of Unix utilities (coreutils, moreutils, grep, findutils), generates Go implementations via an AI code generation pipeline (mage-claude-orchestrator), and verifies correctness through differential testing against GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture**: Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). Key components:\n- `cmd/` — one Go package per utility\n- `pkg/testutils/` — differential testing harness (compares Go binary vs GNU binary)\n- `pkg/sys/` — Darwin/Linux syscall abstractions\n- `pkg/format/` — shared output formatting (column alignment, ANSI colors, human-readable sizes)\n- `magefiles/` — build targets (excluded from generation per DD7)\n- `docs/` — specifications (human-authored, read-only for the pipeline)\n\n**Implementation status**: `pkg/testutils/` exists in source code (difftest.go + tests). All other packages and utilities have no generated code on the working branch. Specs are complete for releases 00.0 through 04.1 (except 02.x which is pending).\n\n**Current release**: Release 00.0 (Batch 0 — foundational infrastructure) is the earliest incomplete release with 4 use cases: uc001-magefiles (excluded by DD7), uc002-format (pending), uc003-sys (pending), uc004-testutils (done — exists in source_code).\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nRelease 00.0 is the earliest incomplete release. Within it:\n- **uc001-magefiles**: Excluded from generation (DD7)\n- **uc004-testutils**: Already implemented (source_code shows difftest.go + difftest_test.go)\n- **uc002-format**: Needs implementation — alphabetically first remaining use case\n- **uc003-sys**: Needs implementation — after format\n\n`pkg/format/` and `pkg/sys/` are independent (format doesn't import sys). By P8's alphabetical tiebreaker, `pkg/format/` comes first. It's needed by `cmd/du` (rel01.3) for human-readable sizes and `cmd/ls` (rel04.0) for colors and column alignment.\n\nI propose one implementation task for `pkg/format/` core functionality. Tests will follow in a separate task per P2.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"Implement pkg/format/ core formatting -- sizes, colors, columns (rel00.0-uc002-format)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (pkg/format/ component -- capabilities and design decisions)\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/ (locate the PRD for pkg/format -- glob for prd*format*.yaml)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel00.0-uc002-format.yaml (use case for the format package)\n      - pkg/testutils/difftest.go (reference for package structure, copyright header, and code style)\n\n    files:\n      - path: pkg/format/size.go\n        action: create\n        note: Human-readable size formatting (bytes to K/M/G/T/P units)\n      - path: pkg/format/color.go\n        action: create\n        note: ANSI color code generation for file types and permissions\n      - path: pkg/format/column.go\n        action: create\n        note: Column alignment for tabular output (ls -l style)\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement human-readable size formatting that converts byte counts to K/M/G/T/P units with appropriate precision per the format PRD. Support both 1024-based (binary) and 1000-based (SI) unit systems if the PRD requires both.\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement ANSI color code output functions for file types (directory, symlink, executable, pipe, socket, block device, char device) and permission display per the format PRD.\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement column alignment for tabular output that handles variable-width data and produces correctly padded columns for ls -l style display per the format PRD.\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"One source file per capability, named after the primary exported type per project convention (P7). Follow the same copyright header and package comment style as pkg/testutils/difftest.go.\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"No dependency on pkg/sys -- format functions accept primitive Go types (int64 for sizes, os.FileMode for colors, string slices for columns) as inputs, not file handles or paths.\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Use io.Writer and fmt.Fprintf patterns for output generation where applicable, following Go standard library conventions.\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"Package compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"Human-readable size formatting correctly converts byte counts from 0 through petabyte scale with appropriate unit selection and decimal precision.\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"ANSI color functions produce correct escape sequences for all file types listed in R2 and reset sequences to terminate color output.\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"Column alignment produces correctly padded output when given variable-width input data across multiple columns.\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"All exported types and functions have Go doc comments following standard Go conventions.\"\n      - id: AC6\n        text: \"pkg/format imports no packages from pkg/sys -- the package is self-contained for formatting logic.\"\n```","stop_reason":null,"session_id":"c059ae7b-fe56-4ca4-b5c4-87f9e4390386","total_cost_usd":0.51018575,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":23741,"cache_read_input_tokens":19289,"output_tokens":14086,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":23741,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":14